---

<Base title="About" description="What Tian is, and who makes it">
  <Prose>
    <h1>Tian</h1>
    <p>
      Tian (天, <i>tiān</i>: day, sky) is a set of games for learning Mandarin
      Chinese, around one word bank: a trip from Beijing to Shanghai in text
      that turns Chinese as you learn, Journey to the West as a role-playing
      game, shadow-puppet stories, tones, pinyin, characters and their
      strokes, and about ten minutes of practice a day. It is made by Gorm
      Rødder, for his family and friends, as part of
      <a href="https://ymse.land">Ymseland</a>.
    </p>
    <p class="text-lg font-semibold"><a href="/">Play Tian</a></p>

    <h2>Signing in</h2>
    <p>
      Everything can be played without signing in. Progress is then kept in
      the browser only. Signed in with Google, anyone keeps the word bank on
      their account, so it follows them to every device. What is stored, and
      where, is in the
      <a href="https://tian.ymse.land/privacy">privacy policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>No ads, no tracking</h2>
    <p>Tian has no advertising, no tracking and no analytics.</p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p><a href="mailto:gorm@ymse.land">gorm@ymse.land</a></p>
  </Prose>
</Base>
